on/id #uuid "63d0ad07-b447-57fc-bb77-4bbdba118ac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-94125" :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms are given in their canonical forms?\n\n- $P(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$\n- $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}$\n- $R(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax,$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form in its canonical form shouldn't contain any cross-product terms (${x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ where $i\\ne j$). In terms of its matrix representation, this means that the corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- $P(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since it contains the cross-product term $2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$\n\n- $Q(x)$ is in canonical form. Indeed, the form does not contain any cross-product terms (it contains only squares).\n\n- $R(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since its corresponding matrix is *not* diagonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q(x)$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94125/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd14a52-8c49-563a-85b2-8d3e4a3f4cff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94125"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94132/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" :answer/id #uuid "aa413377-363a-5358-b6fb-84fb2523b3ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94132/selection/70fa48071bbef29483d5011a085a18a644339fba8eaeeff3743b4f30822d222b" :answer/id #uuid "158c9ef9-2f2c-5ec9-a8c5-cebc53d7532d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ and $R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94132/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" :answer/id #uuid "c1ad7033-0797-5fb5-b1ab-357a8ff3ca68" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94132/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" :answer/id #uuid "cb5b2930-88c5-5cce-9c8f-07359ccd4db3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94132/selection/b7efae5b893065fbc8008c0afd6792d08404fb95a0ae729bdbfc3112d34d8931" :answer/id #uuid "1f991554-fc3e-53e2-8aa1-ccc26f696659" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94132/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5fe962-adbf-5f6c-a85a-09731a4e9412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94132/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" :answer-field/choices ["q-94132/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" "q-94132/selection/70fa48071bbef29483d5011a085a18a644339fba8eaeeff3743b4f30822d222b" "q-94132/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" "q-94132/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" "q-94132/selection/b7efae5b893065fbc8008c0afd6792d08404fb95a0ae729bdbfc3112d34d8931"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94132" :question/id #uuid "ac19d765-c6e4-5363-aff8-6d46d36905da" :question/math-academy-id "q-94132" :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms are given in their canonical forms?\n\n- $P(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}$\n- $Q(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax,$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\n- $R(x)=2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form in its canonical form shouldn't contain any cross-product terms (${x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ where $i\\ne j$). In terms of its matrix representation, this means that the corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- $P(x)$ is in canonical form. Indeed, the form does not contain any cross-product terms (it contains only squares).\n\n- $Q(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since its corresponding matrix is not diagonal.\n\n- $R(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since it contains the cross-product term $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P(x)$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd14a52-8c49-563a-85b2-8d3e4a3f4cff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94135/selection/b7efae5b893065fbc8008c0afd6792d08404fb95a0ae729bdbfc3112d34d8931" :answer/id #uuid "56f01c52-66bc-545e-bb1e-b56d0667e187" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94135/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" :answer/id #uuid "bade8cc7-23b3-58f4-b731-5f8de10dcb50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94135/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" :answer/id #uuid "1f1e28ab-e1c9-5165-b1ac-93f273373e39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94135/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" :answer/id #uuid "49359dd7-70d9-5e3c-9b33-ae6be2c2d4e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94135/selection/b5205baee6bd78e4ab9a6c75b5094a9f701b40fb1ae51bb17f6cafd17f9fb366" :answer/id #uuid "71b3af53-6994-50b9-976c-46b8f4831743" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q(x)$ and $R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94135/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "566e5a81-eefa-5ae8-899f-caa5a7284b2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94135/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" :answer-field/choices ["q-94135/selection/b7efae5b893065fbc8008c0afd6792d08404fb95a0ae729bdbfc3112d34d8931" "q-94135/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" "q-94135/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" "q-94135/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" "q-94135/selection/b5205baee6bd78e4ab9a6c75b5094a9f701b40fb1ae51bb17f6cafd17f9fb366"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94135" :question/id #uuid "e4e32ab9-8f46-5714-bca5-d7cb14182740" :question/math-academy-id "q-94135" :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms are given in their canonical forms?\n\n- $P(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax,$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\n- $Q(x)={x}_{3}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2}$\n- $R(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form in its canonical form shouldn't contain any cross-product terms (${x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ where $i\\ne j$). In terms of its matrix representation, this means that the corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- $P(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since its corresponding matrix is not diagonal.\n\n- $Q(x)$ is in canonical form. Indeed, the form does not contain any cross-product terms (it contains only squares).\n\n- $R(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since it contains the cross-product term ${x}_{1}{x}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q(x)$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94135/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd14a52-8c49-563a-85b2-8d3e4a3f4cff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94135"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140982/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" :answer/id #uuid "6565f6f3-11fb-5380-b898-1fb6f86a80f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140982/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" :answer/id #uuid "a92d617a-4b4e-5add-b0b5-b948f38ab4ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140982/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" :answer/id #uuid "be9417a3-026f-5fa7-bb97-ab92fc702019" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140982/selection/b5205baee6bd78e4ab9a6c75b5094a9f701b40fb1ae51bb17f6cafd17f9fb366" :answer/id #uuid "3f183202-7067-50a8-b0e4-55e7cd79b36f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q(x)$ and $R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140982/selection/b7efae5b893065fbc8008c0afd6792d08404fb95a0ae729bdbfc3112d34d8931" :answer/id #uuid "6b2d48f7-288b-5a3a-b822-317c59a9d1ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140982/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4985610-d461-59e5-89dd-ea940d6b0a2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140982/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" :answer-field/choices ["q-140982/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" "q-140982/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" "q-140982/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" "q-140982/selection/b5205baee6bd78e4ab9a6c75b5094a9f701b40fb1ae51bb17f6cafd17f9fb366" "q-140982/selection/b7efae5b893065fbc8008c0afd6792d08404fb95a0ae729bdbfc3112d34d8931"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140982" :question/id #uuid "36a5116d-e670-58dd-8a1a-da9cc3b98bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-140982" :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms are given in their canonical forms?\n\n- $P(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$\n- $Q(x)=({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}$\n- $R(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax,$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form in its canonical form shouldn't contain any cross-product terms (${x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ where $i\\ne j$). In terms of its matrix representation, this means that the corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- $P(x)$ is in canonical form. Indeed, the form does not contain any cross-product terms (it contains only squares).\n\n- $Q(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since \n\n$$\nQ(x)=({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\n So,  it contains the cross-product term $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}.$\n\n- $R(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since its corresponding matrix is not diagonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P(x)$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140982/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd14a52-8c49-563a-85b2-8d3e4a3f4cff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140982"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94127/selection/70fa48071bbef29483d5011a085a18a644339fba8eaeeff3743b4f30822d222b" :answer/id #uuid "2b351129-799e-5010-84b0-b56ab77e660a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ and $R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94127/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" :answer/id #uuid "fa9952bd-add3-5932-991d-a5b40f2e8c75" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94127/selection/b5205baee6bd78e4ab9a6c75b5094a9f701b40fb1ae51bb17f6cafd17f9fb366" :answer/id #uuid "6fb10cf8-7261-508e-ae05-771e882b1f73" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q(x)$ and $R(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94127/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" :answer/id #uuid "185ed8f4-fd06-593d-98bb-202de626a977" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94127/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" :answer/id #uuid "b96f588b-dc25-570c-ba14-1c51cb2a25e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94127/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d4a88bd-9463-535e-8b04-97d89b49c30f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94127/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6" :answer-field/choices ["q-94127/selection/70fa48071bbef29483d5011a085a18a644339fba8eaeeff3743b4f30822d222b" "q-94127/selection/96ae2bfdf84c45d690b672f8fab02119e8d1347fdf5bd41a64a8b606867be5df" "q-94127/selection/b5205baee6bd78e4ab9a6c75b5094a9f701b40fb1ae51bb17f6cafd17f9fb366" "q-94127/selection/3fb0dc42c03f4b136ea8456f17fdd1961ad65045ade2d3fdb4ba19ef97dd366c" "q-94127/selection/62bb2f2c64686e458fc4a48632a23984479c9e1842b1e945f063e5981a3a34d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94127" :question/id #uuid "6bcaa271-3d5a-59dc-bfa8-3f9708c45d5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94127" :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms are given in their canonical forms?\n\n- $P(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$\n- $Q(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax,$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $R(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form in its canonical form shouldn't contain any cross-product terms (${x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ where $i\\ne j$). In terms of its matrix representation, this means that the corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- $P(x)$ is in canonical form. Indeed, the form does not contain any cross-product terms (it contains only squares).\n\n- $Q(x)$ is in canonical form. Indeed, its corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\n- $R(x)$ is *not* in canonical form since it contains the cross-product term ${x}_{1}{x}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94127/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd14a52-8c49-563a-85b2-8d3e4a3f4cff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94127"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94149/selection/bf3f7a2b496add4a1714ede73c76c62252abca334fcc6ff6d28874751ccb7600" :answer/id #uuid "a4dd6dc8-b571-5f12-91f8-b27a856298aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and ${x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94149/selection/b63be77c216211a808264a07d139c4a4f835987091d8d262ffcc37bb319c3a30" :answer/id #uuid "8ddf4364-5244-5bdd-aa16-ebc15eb6ab10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94149/selection/4c21a51594c473dc51f7db2ee81b87c5ec91c43eaf47bd1f79f6d39d0faf4e98" :answer/id #uuid "afdb44de-b78f-5507-aa8d-c70bfb219802" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94149/selection/8eeecd0bf38cf0f7147b40091d127a46d4613554c719eb240f2ce466d969dc6d" :answer/id #uuid "dfe3adfe-57b7-5d0f-ad71-b8d9794a5244" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94149/selection/198a9b526a7d6ad526fd607d469050acc483f673c9e183786d223e2dda242906" :answer/id #uuid "62c29d18-b7ad-5791-8c03-010ac438d1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94149/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "21ff659b-1664-5cf5-ac6b-8c2df62d69a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94149/selection/198a9b526a7d6ad526fd607d469050acc483f673c9e183786d223e2dda242906" :answer-field/choices ["q-94149/selection/bf3f7a2b496add4a1714ede73c76c62252abca334fcc6ff6d28874751ccb7600" "q-94149/selection/b63be77c216211a808264a07d139c4a4f835987091d8d262ffcc37bb319c3a30" "q-94149/selection/4c21a51594c473dc51f7db2ee81b87c5ec91c43eaf47bd1f79f6d39d0faf4e98" "q-94149/selection/8eeecd0bf38cf0f7147b40091d127a46d4613554c719eb240f2ce466d969dc6d" "q-94149/selection/198a9b526a7d6ad526fd607d469050acc483f673c9e183786d223e2dda242906"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94149" :question/id #uuid "f8717eb0-f4e1-50fd-9190-b8cfaaa41b81" :question/math-academy-id "q-94149" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =(2{x}_{1}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} & =2([{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}]-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} & =2({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-32{x}_{2}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $2\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94149/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c4037e5-607d-5cc4-9ce8-f7f1cd2c5aae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94149"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94142"] :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+29{x}_{2}^{2}+18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+29{x}_{2}^{2}+18{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =(3{x}_{1}^{2}+18{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+29{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+29{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+29{x}_{2}^{2} & =3([{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+9{x}_{2}^{2}]-9{x}_{2}^{2})+29{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3(({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2})+29{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2})+29{x}_{2}^{2} & =3({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})^{2}-27{x}_{2}^{2}+29{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n3{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $3\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94143/selection/8eeecd0bf38cf0f7147b40091d127a46d4613554c719eb240f2ce466d969dc6d" :answer/id #uuid "3cea3095-4069-5aca-a04b-ac1ee4ec0caa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94143/selection/a8fe2f4acc9252c5fffd4ac6641d16a80054f1c05178e6f996bd061f2220e302" :answer/id #uuid "120dc73c-da7e-50d0-b3cb-4b9dbf033862" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ and ${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94143/selection/0198a1b6d2d5a44d97d7b3f857e0c5b909a7b8a7f154128ca36221eb1d881850" :answer/id #uuid "0a5579d2-55b9-50e5-8fde-8384a84cbe16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94143/selection/35558fba997edba4985df766ed9b9343320c6647a21dacb083410ef8d1fc30b9" :answer/id #uuid "854e487c-4182-5f10-b727-ee195380e695" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94143/selection/ead7345500d5edc9906a75bd17be88bc12baea1a451edce7880b1e76f3fca5bc" :answer/id #uuid "4a742eab-a8f5-5273-a63b-7b0fcb8c396d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94143/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1568567-5c21-55e2-949c-92784f07ef65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94143/selection/35558fba997edba4985df766ed9b9343320c6647a21dacb083410ef8d1fc30b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-94143/selection/8eeecd0bf38cf0f7147b40091d127a46d4613554c719eb240f2ce466d969dc6d" "q-94143/selection/a8fe2f4acc9252c5fffd4ac6641d16a80054f1c05178e6f996bd061f2220e302" "q-94143/selection/0198a1b6d2d5a44d97d7b3f857e0c5b909a7b8a7f154128ca36221eb1d881850" "q-94143/selection/35558fba997edba4985df766ed9b9343320c6647a21dacb083410ef8d1fc30b9" "q-94143/selection/ead7345500d5edc9906a75bd17be88bc12baea1a451edce7880b1e76f3fca5bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94143" :question/id #uuid "403b4989-6bac-5fe3-925c-98de701e3311" :question/math-academy-id "q-94143" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n3{y}_{1}^{2}+\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =(3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} & =3([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} & =3({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n3{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $2\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94143/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c4037e5-607d-5cc4-9ce8-f7f1cd2c5aae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94143"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94139/selection/855fcdef3c05bf531b121667412bab50d877326aafbc21dffed90b84b8f81132" :answer/id #uuid "3bff65ef-68b3-591a-9cc4-fea0df0d6343" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94139/selection/36b477db6c0ea09240de955f019a986877310ac797db72a1fe46b05c656cab60" :answer/id #uuid "a61c089e-855c-5bc9-b034-517a3d1b718f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94139/selection/d86f2db6c9fb0772ff4cc9e790e96369ec0f6a57358f1055b74b49f05e3f85cc" :answer/id #uuid "90319618-999c-56ff-95f5-70bbc008f51a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94139/selection/a63cdb1d6c267981c56eb9be076cd2e4c3af6e96e1df5736f9d22f6f5a15a8af" :answer/id #uuid "a21ae77c-2ca6-515f-80ab-946786a909b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94139/selection/969e41c7b66ee5454dde578249ed059916ded3338e6a54d6ca56023af21e12a9" :answer/id #uuid "96d30665-c1f2-5163-b85d-34307ec4254a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and ${x}_{2}-{x}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94139/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60347550-5557-5b74-b1fd-70e810ae5ac1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94139/selection/36b477db6c0ea09240de955f019a986877310ac797db72a1fe46b05c656cab60" :answer-field/choices ["q-94139/selection/855fcdef3c05bf531b121667412bab50d877326aafbc21dffed90b84b8f81132" "q-94139/selection/36b477db6c0ea09240de955f019a986877310ac797db72a1fe46b05c656cab60" "q-94139/selection/d86f2db6c9fb0772ff4cc9e790e96369ec0f6a57358f1055b74b49f05e3f85cc" "q-94139/selection/a63cdb1d6c267981c56eb9be076cd2e4c3af6e96e1df5736f9d22f6f5a15a8af" "q-94139/selection/969e41c7b66ee5454dde578249ed059916ded3338e6a54d6ca56023af21e12a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94139" :question/id #uuid "106b083d-c143-5f48-8526-3cd804d072e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-94139" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+7{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}+7{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n9{y}_{1}^{2}+7{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $9\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94139/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c4037e5-607d-5cc4-9ce8-f7f1cd2c5aae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94139"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94138/selection/0198a1b6d2d5a44d97d7b3f857e0c5b909a7b8a7f154128ca36221eb1d881850" :answer/id #uuid "5afdfeec-a314-50e6-a60e-783eb6ac0929" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94138/selection/35558fba997edba4985df766ed9b9343320c6647a21dacb083410ef8d1fc30b9" :answer/id #uuid "292cce09-6793-50b8-bc54-dab5a48c3014" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94138/selection/b63be77c216211a808264a07d139c4a4f835987091d8d262ffcc37bb319c3a30" :answer/id #uuid "0f2d282d-70cb-5802-a891-07cce3420428" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94138/selection/8eeecd0bf38cf0f7147b40091d127a46d4613554c719eb240f2ce466d969dc6d" :answer/id #uuid "55ed7227-a241-5096-9dc6-a193393aee0f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94138/selection/cb46c1c9622eb92571f631dd260003cc4aad08867b02b88f302ac5fc1e0afd16" :answer/id #uuid "56b9fab5-cff2-5750-a0cc-2f3e3254d0da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94138/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9dba355-9e75-5ab3-af62-8644c7fe96fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94138/selection/b63be77c216211a808264a07d139c4a4f835987091d8d262ffcc37bb319c3a30" :answer-field/choices ["q-94138/selection/0198a1b6d2d5a44d97d7b3f857e0c5b909a7b8a7f154128ca36221eb1d881850" "q-94138/selection/35558fba997edba4985df766ed9b9343320c6647a21dacb083410ef8d1fc30b9" "q-94138/selection/b63be77c216211a808264a07d139c4a4f835987091d8d262ffcc37bb319c3a30" "q-94138/selection/8eeecd0bf38cf0f7147b40091d127a46d4613554c719eb240f2ce466d969dc6d" "q-94138/selection/cb46c1c9622eb92571f631dd260003cc4aad08867b02b88f302ac5fc1e0afd16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94138" :question/id #uuid "114299ac-5cb6-5ace-82c7-9724e64c9935" :question/math-academy-id "q-94138" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(4{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =4([{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =4({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n4{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $4\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94138/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c4037e5-607d-5cc4-9ce8-f7f1cd2c5aae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94162/selection/6be1d253f35f1e230f1cbb1daefebfd649e2c96e902759ab1e79e1fe8318ae69" :answer/id #uuid "31655740-43d9-5ecb-af5b-a698bf0f1845" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94162/selection/155a55e708c9842ffdebcafa6af64714ad50c53594a2581d3557bc1ee02f7637" :answer/id #uuid "25861e5e-a39f-5c2b-b4c7-a2dd1011be87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94162/selection/14d0087cc5642b9e92d39409a471f5a312a0fe14d9eaa542aab8be439f8d78d8" :answer/id #uuid "f9fb1b5b-e38f-5219-949e-695d79d77720" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94162/selection/75c7cda466e5237e1005636c6d35f70202f3f38fa6bcb17e3494e007aa42984f" :answer/id #uuid "7c8713ec-b85f-52f9-9428-09c640f0d2b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94162/selection/f1d6475bd29a4d1f875d4dc2867aa3934b5ef8125b7b1b6f123dd4bcb72d25be" :answer/id #uuid "839e541a-ffe0-509c-9cbc-294da6944c48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94162/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63e491cd-1a78-50e4-8539-4a3c697daa2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94162/selection/f1d6475bd29a4d1f875d4dc2867aa3934b5ef8125b7b1b6f123dd4bcb72d25be" :answer-field/choices ["q-94162/selection/6be1d253f35f1e230f1cbb1daefebfd649e2c96e902759ab1e79e1fe8318ae69" "q-94162/selection/155a55e708c9842ffdebcafa6af64714ad50c53594a2581d3557bc1ee02f7637" "q-94162/selection/14d0087cc5642b9e92d39409a471f5a312a0fe14d9eaa542aab8be439f8d78d8" "q-94162/selection/75c7cda466e5237e1005636c6d35f70202f3f38fa6bcb17e3494e007aa42984f" "q-94162/selection/f1d6475bd29a4d1f875d4dc2867aa3934b5ef8125b7b1b6f123dd4bcb72d25be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94162" :question/id #uuid "ad6201ba-6d80-5b8d-a89d-c34d502e4eae" :question/math-academy-id "q-94162" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+{x}_{3}))+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2})+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3})-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+([{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}]-{x}_{3}^{2})-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94162/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e5e149-54cd-528e-b50e-1cafecb7b77a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94162"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94179/selection/b12ba70fb54264da9f4f976aae2ae6c48b5edcadff56d1f0c77137793768873b" :answer/id #uuid "87e56994-33b9-5413-b9ba-b4da3cc0e961" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94179/selection/1663bd069d426bb6b27ad15bfced764ccbf09135b964dae4387f0553f4778029" :answer/id #uuid "2d9459cd-b222-5323-883b-3b14adea5308" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94179/selection/52436ed0be8b8262c7e25a262fafc9f4df793d4102fc8fdbcad6d0bb6eb876a1" :answer/id #uuid "06a59861-c8de-534f-b615-879a840fc325" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94179/selection/6c49dc6e6fde0e463a0dd76678abef7025c8def99b8736a97186b51e2a63c959" :answer/id #uuid "c752445e-f9e7-5e41-bd24-3e894263dc3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94179/selection/155a55e708c9842ffdebcafa6af64714ad50c53594a2581d3557bc1ee02f7637" :answer/id #uuid "c3a6c54f-054a-53e4-8bcb-85f546bb68d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94179/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1edfafcd-d14c-52c4-9ccf-93835779a290" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94179/selection/b12ba70fb54264da9f4f976aae2ae6c48b5edcadff56d1f0c77137793768873b" :answer-field/choices ["q-94179/selection/b12ba70fb54264da9f4f976aae2ae6c48b5edcadff56d1f0c77137793768873b" "q-94179/selection/1663bd069d426bb6b27ad15bfced764ccbf09135b964dae4387f0553f4778029" "q-94179/selection/52436ed0be8b8262c7e25a262fafc9f4df793d4102fc8fdbcad6d0bb6eb876a1" "q-94179/selection/6c49dc6e6fde0e463a0dd76678abef7025c8def99b8736a97186b51e2a63c959" "q-94179/selection/155a55e708c9842ffdebcafa6af64714ad50c53594a2581d3557bc1ee02f7637"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94179" :question/id #uuid "c34790ce-c36b-5dcb-a189-d84001cf999a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94179" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3}))+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2([{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2(({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{3}^{2}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e5e149-54cd-528e-b50e-1cafecb7b77a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94161/selection/3df4f1c0ad0619123ce617f18bf81ca46d69924022da76ec9cdf17195061c383" :answer/id #uuid "5cdc41f5-49de-5f52-9549-21fd321502d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/va