ange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}))-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2})-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-25{x}_{2}^{2}+10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94161/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e5e149-54cd-528e-b50e-1cafecb7b77a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94161"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94159/selection/4483bf05